* js/localization/strings/fr.js

Read the relevant documentation in ALVA_SPEC.md before modifying the interface.

2. Show difficulty in EVERY roster

All fighter-selection interfaces must display the selected or previewed fighter’s difficulty stars.

This includes:

1. Discover → Fighters
2. Quick Battle → Select Fighter
3. Custom Play → Select CPU
4. Watch Mode → Select CPU 1
5. Watch Mode → Select CPU 2
6. Practice Ground → Change Fighter
7. Practice Ground → Select CPU / Change CPU

Important: Implement this through shared roster UI code so that future roster instances automatically inherit the feature.

Difficulty presentation

Use ALVA’s existing five-star rating system.

Examples based on current fighter profiles:

* #0001: ★★★★★
* #0002: ★★★☆☆

Rules:

* Display exactly five stars.
* Filled stars represent the character’s existing difficulty rating.
* Unfilled stars remain visible.
* Maintain ALVA’s existing star styling and colors.
* Do not introduce another difficulty calculation or rating system.
* Display the rating in the preview information area, near the fighter’s name.
* Update the rating immediately when the previewed fighter changes.

REMOVE the visible “Difficulty” label

The current Discover interface displays:

DIFFICULTY ★★★★★

Change this to:

★★★★★

Remove the visible word “Difficulty” entirely from beside the stars on every roster.

Do not replace it with another visible heading or indicator.

However, retain an accessible description such as “Difficulty: 5 out of 5 stars” for screen readers. The stars should remain informational and non-interactive.

Do not confuse fighter difficulty ratings with Quick Battle’s separate CPU difficulty selection.

3. Rename the play-style action

The current button says:

Play style description

Change it everywhere to exactly:

Read play style

Requirements:

* Update the existing localization key rather than hardcoding text in individual screens.
* Update English and French translations.
* Use a natural French equivalent such as “Lire le style de jeu”.
* Keep the existing modal’s title, “Play style”, unless a change is needed for consistency.
* Do not rewrite or shorten the actual character descriptions.
* Ensure the action updates correctly when the game’s language changes.

4. Make “Read play style” smaller

The current .text-action styling uses a 12px font.

Reduce the visible text size slightly, targeting approximately 11px.

Design requirements:

* Smaller than the current text.
* Subtle and secondary to the fighter’s name and difficulty stars.
* Maintain the existing understated, underlined text-button appearance.
* Use ALVA’s existing typography and color variables.
* Preserve readable contrast.
* Keep a comfortable clickable/tappable area despite the smaller font.
* Preserve hover, active, keyboard-focus, and gamepad-focus states.

The action should feel like a small informational link, not a primary button.

5. Move “Read play style” to the BOTTOM RIGHT

Currently, Discover places the play-style action on the same horizontal row as the difficulty rating.

This arrangement must change.

New layout

Organize the fighter preview information so that:

* Difficulty stars appear near the top-left of the information area.
* The fighter’s name remains prominently displayed.
* “Read play style” appears at the bottom-right corner of the preview information area.
* The action is right-aligned and visually separated from the difficulty stars.
* It must not sit next to the stars anymore.

